Third-party material in this repository
---------------------------------------
Microsoft's security baselines: none.
  The kit applies the Microsoft Security Baselines for Windows 11 and for
  Microsoft Edge (part of the Microsoft Security Compliance Toolkit,
  (c) Microsoft Corporation), but it ships none of them. The repository holds
  only each baseline's official download address, file name and SHA-256, the
  names and order of its policy objects, and the identifiers of the policy
  extensions Microsoft's installer registers (config/baselines/). At build time
  the kit downloads Microsoft's own files from Microsoft
  (https://www.microsoft.com/download/details.aspx?id=55319) to your PC and
  reads the settings from them there (scripts/Import-Baseline.py). All rights
  in the baselines remain with Microsoft.

docs/dev/reviews/STIG-REVIEW.md, docs/dev/reviews/STIG-REVIEW-rules.csv
  Rule identifiers, titles and severity categories from the "Microsoft Windows
  11 Security Technical Implementation Guide", Version 2, Release 11
  (UNCLASSIFIED; developed by the U.S. Defense Information Systems Agency and
  publicly available at https://public.cyber.mil/). A work of the U.S.
  Government. The comparison is this project's own static review. It is not a
  STIG assessment, and nothing here is STIG-compliant, validated or approved.
  DISA accepts no liability for the consequences of applying STIG settings and
  does not endorse this project.

CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md refers to the Contributor Covenant 2.1
  (https://www.contributor-covenant.org), CC BY 4.0. Its text is not copied.

